episode four of loki was the most  revealing and game-changing installment  yet  the episode also had some treats in  store for marvel comics fans and  mcu diehards here are a few easter eggs  you may have missed in loki episode 4.  one of the biggest surprises to come in  episode 4 is the return of jaime  alexander as  lady siff we haven't seen the character  in the mcu since 2013's thor the dark  world  and while we suspected the missing hero  might be returning her appearance was  still shocking nonetheless  sif's cameo was brief and those  unfamiliar with norse mythology might  have missed a famous story hiding in  plain sight  when she first encounters loki siff is  holding a lock of her dark hair  she charges at loki beyond aggravated  that he cut off her tresses  and calls him pathetic and conniving in  addition to other  unpleasant words she aggressively knees  and punches him  and loki has to relive the event over  and over as he's stuck in a time loop  while it might seem like a storyline the  loki writers conjured up  they actually pulled it directly from  the two characters mythologies  in the norse myths unlike the mcu siff  is known for her long golden hair  in the myths loki cuts off sip's hair  which puts thor her husband  in a fit of rage after his brother  charges him with replacing her hair  loki travels to nedevalier where  stormbreaker was forged in infinity war  so the dwarves can create  new hair for sif out of gold which would  grow once placed on her head  we finally get a look at the time  keepers in episode 4 after their  appearances were teased with tva  sculptures throughout earlier episodes  of the series  when loki and sylvie are brought before  them to be pruned  the time keepers give them a chance to  speak we don't get much out of these  mysterious beings although their disdain  for the loki variants is obvious  with the help of hunter b15 who's had  her memories of her pre-tva life  restored by sylvie  the loki's are able to battle and defeat  their captors  and sylvie severs the head of a  timekeeper only to discover that they're  just  androids beyond disappointed loki and  sylvia are left wondering who created  the tva  marvel comics might have some answers  the timekeepers first appeared in 1979's  thor number 282 and were created by he  who remains someone unmentioned during  episode 4.  also known as him who remains or more  simply him  this mystery being was the last director  of the tva who put the timekeepers in  place to oversee the organization  originally him created the time twisters  in 1976's thorn number 243  another trio of beings who strayed from  their directive and began destroying  earth every 3000 years  in loki the time looping devices used by  the tva are known as  time twisters in an apparent nod to  these characters  or the time twister just loops you not  the furniture  while we don't know who specifically  created the tva in the world of loki  he who remains or the time twisters  might have some insight  different versions of loki are teased in  episode 2 during a briefing mobius gives  to a group of minutemen and other tva  workers before they take off to oshkosh  wisconsin  these variants are displayed on a  hologram which depicts five different  versions of the character  none of these guys however match the  four new loki's we meet in the episode  four mid-credit scene  thanks to the credits we know these  variants are boastful loki  classic loki and kid loki oh yeah there  is also a crocodile loki  classic loki sports the traditional garb  the character war when he first appeared  in 1962's journey into mystery number  85.  kid loki has a much shorter history in  the comics first appearing in 2010's  thor  number 617 this incarnation came about  after the original loki  died but he was reborn as a child who  eventually joins the young avengers  the backgrounds on our other two  variants are vague but boastful loki's  possession of a hammer could be a nod to  2020's thorn number four  in this comic thor's brother is able to  lift mjolnir while on yottenheim  loki was also able to lift mjolnir  during marvel's axis event when his  moral alignment was reversed which made  him the god of  heroism comic precedents aside boastful  loki's appearance at least hints at some  sort of confirmation that a loki variant  is worthy  as far as the crocodile goes there seems  to be no history of this character in  the comics  we've seen a frog version of thor before  aka throg the frog of thunder in 2009's  lockjaw and the pet avengers number one  and loki turns thor into a frog in thor  number 363.  so hey why not a crocodile loki  after loki gets pruned he winds up in  new york city where he meets his new  variant buddies  most of the focus in the scene is on the  new loki's and while your eyes are drawn  to a crocodile wearing gold horns  there's something major you might have  missed in the background avengers tower  previously known as stark tower is  looming in the distance  absolutely destroyed we've seen the  building take a beating before but  nothing like this the new loki's appear  to be hiding out in another apocalyptic  event  although this time it seems to have  already happened as opposed to previous  episodes when the events were imminent  avengers tower is decimated in this  timeline with its top floor balconies  obliterated as it rests on a tilt  it looks like the barn door protocol  wasn't installed on this former  superhero hangout  like it was for avengers hq in end game  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  loki are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

